1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:02,310
Morning, how you doing?

2
00:00:02,648 --> 00:00:03,648
Me too!

3
00:00:04,891 --> 00:00:06,601
Everyone here says they're fine.

4
00:00:06,651 --> 00:00:08,391
Now you can see their weather.

5
00:00:08,685 --> 00:00:09,785
Except yours.

6
00:00:10,614 --> 00:00:11,444
Rule one.

7
00:00:11,494 --> 00:00:13,314
You can see everyone's inner weather.

8
00:00:13,629 --> 00:00:14,459
Morning!

9
00:00:14,509 --> 00:00:16,041
Doing great!

10
00:00:16,091 --> 00:00:17,591
He was not doing great.

11
00:00:17,899 --> 00:00:18,569
Rule two.

12
00:00:18,619 --> 00:00:19,545
They can't.

13
00:00:19,595 --> 00:00:20,595
What cloud?

14
00:00:20,670 --> 00:00:21,500
Rule three.

15
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:23,770
The only weather you can't see is your own.

16
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:28,220
And you've had a week.

17
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:31,290
Yours is probably the biggest storm on the island.

18
00:00:32,497 --> 00:00:35,087
Guess how many people down there are having a hard week.

19
00:00:35,137 --> 00:00:36,137
Go on.

20
00:00:40,246 --> 00:00:45,346
People consistently underestimate how often others are going through hard times.

21
00:00:45,482 --> 00:00:51,302
Even close friends tended to underestimate how much negative emotion someone was feeling.

22
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:53,850
So why does everyone look so fine?

23
00:00:56,283 --> 00:00:57,433
Ahoy!

24
00:00:57,483 --> 00:00:58,983
Lovely day for it!

25
00:00:59,835 --> 00:01:00,585
Morning!

26
00:01:00,635 --> 00:01:03,175
Fresh rolls, still warm!

27
00:01:05,296 --> 00:01:09,676
People report hiding their bad feelings far more often than their good ones.

28
00:01:09,863 --> 00:01:13,363
Which means the biggest storms are the ones nobody shows.

29
00:01:14,027 --> 00:01:16,327
So you decide to fix everyone's weather.

30
00:01:17,675 --> 00:01:18,345
Oh!

31
00:01:18,395 --> 00:01:19,895
Thank you, Ana!

32
00:01:20,881 --> 00:01:21,711
Can't stop!

33
00:01:21,761 --> 00:01:22,761
I'm fine!

34
00:01:29,532 --> 00:01:30,182
Oops!

35
00:01:30,232 --> 00:01:31,162
oops.

36
00:01:31,212 --> 00:01:32,872
I'm fine, really.

37
00:01:33,214 --> 00:01:36,714
The one helping everyone has the biggest storm on the island.

38
00:01:38,163 --> 00:01:40,273
She said she's fine.

39
00:01:40,323 --> 00:01:41,343
Leave it.

40
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:42,910
You know what fine means now.

41
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:44,430
So you ask one more time.

42
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:45,480
Gently.

43
00:01:47,512 --> 00:01:48,502
I'm fine!

44
00:01:48,552 --> 00:01:49,552
Really!

45
00:01:49,698 --> 00:01:50,958
How are you, really?

46
00:01:51,707 --> 00:01:54,537
Mum's moving off the island on Saturday.

47
00:01:54,587 --> 00:01:57,177
I'm packing the whole house.

48
00:01:57,227 --> 00:01:58,697
By myself.

49
00:01:58,747 --> 00:02:00,807
I didn't want to bother anyone.

50
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:02,510
You tell her to ask.

51
00:02:03,941 --> 00:02:06,051
Nobody's free on a Saturday.

52
00:02:06,101 --> 00:02:09,601
I'd have to ask all twenty of them to get even a couple.

53
00:02:14,051 --> 00:02:16,751
Would anyone be able to help on Saturday?

54
00:02:17,205 --> 00:02:18,090
Of course.

55
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:20,006
I'll bring sandwiches.

56
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:21,316
I've got a van.

57
00:02:22,671 --> 00:02:27,261
In one experiment, people guessed they'd have to ask about twenty strangers to get five

58
00:02:27,311 --> 00:02:28,861
to do a small favor.

59
00:02:28,911 --> 00:02:30,491
They needed about ten.

60
00:02:30,708 --> 00:02:35,088
When people ask strangers for help, more people say yes than they expect.

61
00:02:36,450 --> 00:02:37,360
What about you?

62
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:38,830
How are you, really?

63
00:02:43,307 --> 00:02:43,977
A cloud.

64
00:02:44,027 --> 00:02:44,857
Not the biggest.

65
00:02:44,907 --> 00:02:45,977
Not the smallest.

66
00:02:46,027 --> 00:02:47,687
Just weather, like everyone's.

67
00:02:48,238 --> 00:02:51,978
We may think we're more alone in our hard times than we really are.

68
00:02:52,558 --> 00:02:55,418
And for the first time all week, you don't say fine.

69
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:02,367
On Saturday, the boxes weigh a lot less.

70
00:03:05,723 --> 00:03:07,623
Morning, how you doing?

71
00:03:10,011 --> 00:03:11,801
You'll never see anyone's weather.

72
00:03:11,851 --> 00:03:16,761
But you can ask how someone's doing, and if they say fine, ask one more time.

73
00:03:16,811 --> 00:03:19,881
And if you're the one under the storm, let someone help.

74
00:03:19,931 --> 00:03:22,391
More people say yes than you'd expect.

75
00:03:24,413 --> 00:03:26,123
Everyone's carrying some weather.

76
00:03:26,173 --> 00:03:27,853
You don't have to carry yours alone.
